WEBVTT

00:19:58.145 --> 00:20:01.208
who is a great economist
who is dominating the world these days.

00:20:01.232 --> 00:20:02.403
And what he shows

00:20:02.427 --> 00:20:05.058
is that the neighborhood
you happen to be growing up in

00:20:05.082 --> 00:20:08.105
is a powerful predictor
of how you do in life, the neighborhood.

00:20:08.129 --> 00:20:10.878
So, for example --
this is Eric Klinenberg's research --

00:20:10.902 --> 00:20:12.663
there was a heatwave in Chicago.

00:20:12.687 --> 00:20:16.488
Two neighborhoods, one across the street
from each other, completely identical.

00:20:16.512 --> 00:20:18.778
In one, lots of old people
died in the heatwave.

00:20:18.802 --> 00:20:21.933
In the other, nobody died.
What was the difference?

00:20:21.957 --> 00:20:23.591
One neighborhood had a library.

00:20:23.615 --> 00:20:25.774
In the library, people got
to meet each other.

00:20:25.798 --> 00:20:28.339
And if they could make
social contact with each other,

00:20:28.363 --> 00:20:31.036
when there was a heatwave,
they checked on the old people